Properties of inheritance:
Inheritance is recursive - class A can extend class B, which extends class C....

Inheritance is transitive - if A extends B and B extends C thus C also extends A ( no need to use the extend word again)

In java - each class can be the super-class to unlimited number of classes (doesn't apply to primitives)
however each class can extend at most one class.

The object class- Every class in java extends java.lang.Object, implicitly
or transitively.
The object class itself is the only java class that doesnt extend any other class

